"""Regression test: country_laws_ir must keep raw text and source_url.

Runs the IR normalizer (load_local_source + build_corpus) on a local raw municipal pack
(default: the DK pack) and checks, per corpus row against its raw law/article row:
  1. source_url is non-empty wherever raw has one (and equals it, stripped);
  2. date wraps 'DD-MM-\\nYYYY' in raw survive in the IR body (year kept after the date);
  3. no non-whitespace content is lost: whitespace-stripped IR body == whitespace-stripped raw
     text, else every difference is classified character by character; only the documented
     normalizations in ALLOWED pass (true page stamps, N/M footers, underscore rules, stray
     combining marks, invisible chars, decoded HTML entities). Dash / NFKC / dot-leader / accent
     changes fail, and so do (v3) numero folds ('No. 7' -> 'nr. 7') and any dropped content line
     (site-chrome keyword lines such as 'Home', 'Index', 'CONTENTS', 'All rights reserved', lone
     letters 'v' / 'x' / 'II'), which v3 keeps unless COUNTRY_LAWS_IR_LEGACY_STRIP=1;
  4. CASES: lone numbers that continue a sentence ('juni' + '2026', 'efter' + '1997', 'Bilag' + '4')
     survive in the law row and its article rows;
  5. paragraph breaks (patch v3): every run of blank lines in raw is exactly one blank line in the
     IR body. The IR body has no run of 2+ blank lines and no leading/trailing blank line; every
     raw break between two kept characters is kept, and the IR has no break the raw lacks. Allowed:
     a break inside a hyphen join ('Miljø-\n\nog' -> 'Miljø-og') and a break next to a removed
     line at the very start or end of the text.
  v3.2 additions:
  6. no content line is lost or joined: raw lines are aligned with IR lines (whitespace-insensitive);
     a raw line that is missing in the IR must be page furniture or a fill-in rule line, and IR lines
     made of several raw lines are only allowed for a hyphenated word ('non-' + 'resident'), never for
     single letters ('M' / 'C' / 'R' / 'D' -> 'MCRD') or a list marker ('ways-' + 'a)');
  7. honest paragraph-break accounting: raw breaks = kept + merged (2 -> 1 where a removed line sat
     between two blank-line runs) + hyphen_join + dropped_edge + lost; IR breaks = kept + invented;
  8. CASES_V32: real snippets (IE / LU / GR / SK) for the v3.2 rules, checked with --cases.
  v3.3 additions:
  9. a hyphen join is allowed only when the next word (up to whitespace) starts with a letter and has 2+ letters (never a single letter)
     and, across a blank line, the line ending in the hyphen is a prose line (20+ characters and 3+ words
     of 2+ letters); other joins count as bad_join ('lave-' / 'faciles', '12.0 m-' / 't');
 10. CASES_V33: the LU table-cell joins, the real IE / LU word joins and the single-letter rule.
  v3.4 additions:
 11. a removed lone number counts as page_stamp_line only under the v3.4 rule (_page_stamp_vetoes mirrors
     structure._page_stamp_vetoes): it starts the text or follows a sentence end, has no other lone number within
     12 non-blank lines (columns: ToC / figure lists / tables are kept whole), no list marker or '.' / ')' after it,
     no leading 0, fits rising page order, and is not a 2-9 paragraph number without n-1 / n-2 before it;
     any other removed lone number is lost_lone_number (content);
 12. CASES_V34: real LU snippets (ToC and figure-list columns, house number, '1' of '13)', tariff and subsidy cells,
     lone 0, 'entamée de' + '3', paragraph number, and three true page stamps that must still go);
 13. CASES_V34_NUMREM: all 321 lone-number removals the Verifier listed for LU IR 176b86b271
     (lu_ir_176b_numrem.tsv), with the v3.4.1 expectation; checked against raw with --numrem.
  v3.4.1 additions:
 14. the page-stamp mirror also keeps footnote numbers (a lower-case word of 3+ letters or a closing mark
     directly followed by n, e.g. 'renvoyé1.', or a line starting with n directly followed by a letter,
     e.g. '1ART. 47 bis'), an unconfirmed 1 (not the last line, no lone 2 within 150 lines after it), a
     repeated page number (page numbers never repeat), sign / limit values (line before names a sign or
     limit) and impossible page positions (k >= 150 n, or k < 5 (n - 1) in a text of 150+ non-blank lines);
 15. CASES_V341: real LU snippets for the 10 content lines of the Verifier's 5bc8 review (footnote numbers in
     2f7b, 7a81, 4d41, 7f3e and the sign value '70' in 298a, law row and article copy) and its 2 allowed
     removals ('42' in 8654, first-line '4' in e7ae); CASES_V34 'lu_page_stamp_mid_298a' now expects '70' kept;
 16. CASES_V341_REVIEW: the 32 rows of lu_ir_5bc8_numrem_review.tsv with the Verifier's verdict and the v3.4.1
     outcome; all 10 content rows must be kept; checked with --numrem.
  v3.4.2 additions:
 17. the page-stamp mirror also keeps a page reference: a lone number that is not the first non-blank line and whose
     line before ends in a page word ('Σελ.', 'σελ.', 'Σελίδα', 'p.', 'pp.', 'S.', 'Seite', 'str.', 'page') or
     contains a dot leader ('..' or '…') anywhere; a removed one is lost_lone_number (content);
 18. a line made only of soft hyphens (U+00AD) is kept exactly as written (GR bullet glyphs); emptying it would be an
     invented paragraph break, which item 5 fails;
 19. CASES_V342: real GR snippets (ToC page reference '26' after '......Σελ.' in 4705-wjylweb, U+00AD bullets in
     4705-wchwweb, the 4701-6sarwj2 art-18 copy normalized on its own (no parent), a page stamp after '..' kept in
     1201-9hkow10, '&amp;' decoded to '&' in 1201-6snzw10).
  v3.4.3 additions:
 20. an article row is normalized with its law row's raw text as parent (normalize_legal_text(text, parent=law_text)):
     when the article's non-blank lines occur as one contiguous run of the law's lines, every line the law row's cleanup
     keeps is kept in the article copy too. The article copy never removes a line its law row keeps. Without a parent
     (or without a match) the result is exactly the v3.4.2 result;
 21. CASES_V343: the three footnote numbers the Verifier found dropped from GR article copies while the law row keeps
     them ('31' in 4701-6sarwj2 art-18, '32' in art-30, '1' in 2401-ww82w96 art-6). Each case carries an excerpt of the
     raw law text as "parent"; the number must be kept with the parent, and the parent excerpt must keep it itself.
  Known limit: lines are aligned with difflib, which can misalign long repeated blocks (GR 3701-ada-ctxdwji-l1d:
  the same paragraphs repeated with different page stamps). Such a row is reported as lost_line / paragraph lost
  although nothing is lost; the GR IR README gives the paragraph-level proof for that row.
Usage: python test_text_preservation.py [RAW_PACK_DIR] [--json OUT]
       python test_text_preservation.py --cases
       python test_text_preservation.py --numrem RAW_REPO@REV|RAW_PACK_DIR [--json OUT]
       python test_text_preservation.py --hub IR_REPO@REV|LOCAL_RELEASE_DIR RAW_REPO@REV [--json OUT]
Needs PYTHONPATH pointing at the ipfs_datasets_py checkout (country_laws_ir importable).
"""
from __future__ import annotations
import difflib, html, json, os, re, sys, unicodedata, collections
from pathlib import Path

try:
    from country_laws_ir.normalize import build_corpus, load_local_source
except ImportError:
    from ipfs_datasets_py.processors.legal_scrapers.country_laws_ir.normalize import build_corpus, load_local_source

DATE_WRAP = re.compile(r"(\d{1,2}[-./]\d{1,2}[-./])[ \t]*\n\s*((?:19|20)\d{2})\b")
LONE_NUM = re.compile(r"\d{1,4}")
N_OF_M = re.compile(r"\d{1,3}\s*/\s*\d{1,3}")
SENT_END = re.compile(r"[.!?;][)\]}\"'\u00bb\u201d\u2019]*\s*$")  # v3.2: ':' does not end a sentence
MAX_PAGE_LINES = 150  # v3.2: page-run neighbours are at most this many non-blank lines per page apart
RULE_LINE = re.compile(r"_{3,}(?:\s+_{3,})*")
LIST_MARKER = re.compile(r"[^\W\d_]{1,4}[).](?:\s|$)")


PROSE_MIN_CHARS, PROSE_MIN_WORDS = 20, 3  # v3.3, mirrors structure._is_prose_line


def _is_prose(line: str) -> bool:
    line = (line or "").strip()
    return len(line) >= PROSE_MIN_CHARS and len(re.findall(r"[^\W\d_]{2,}", line)) >= PROSE_MIN_WORDS


def _hyphen_join_ok(prev: str, nxt: str, across_blank: bool) -> bool:
    """v3.3 rule for a line ending in a hyphen glued to the next line (prev / nxt: stripped lines)."""
    word = re.match(r"\S*", nxt or "").group(0)
    return bool(re.search(r"(?<=[^\W\d_])[-‐‑]$", prev or "") and re.match(r"[^\W\d_]", word)
                and len(re.findall(r"[^\W\d_]", word)) >= 2 and not word[0].isupper() and not LIST_MARKER.match(nxt)
                and (not across_blank or _is_prose(prev)))


def _orig_lines(text: str) -> list[tuple[str, bool]]:
    """Non-blank lines (stripped, same order as _para_lines keys) with a 'blank line before' flag."""
    out, blank = [], False
    for ln in _BREAK_SPLIT.sub("\n", text or "").split("\n"):
        if not _ws(ln):
            blank = True
            continue
        out.append((ln.strip(), blank)); blank = False
    return out


def _ends_sentence(prev: str) -> bool:
    return bool(SENT_END.search(prev) and re.search(r"\w", prev))
# Lone numbers that continue a sentence must survive (verifier cases, DK raw 6cde55bae0):
# (law id, raw pattern); checked in the law row and every article row of that law.
CASES = [
    ("dk-mun-621-2981", r"udgangen af juni\s*\n\s*2026"),
    ("dk-mun-183-1691", r"før og efter\s*\n\s*1997"),
    ("dk-mun-479-2692", r"beskrevet i Bilag\s*\n\s*4\b"),
]
# Documented IR normalizations; stored text is otherwise kept character for character:
#   page_stamp_line    v3.4: a lone page number that starts the text or whose previous line ends a
#                      sentence, and that no rule of _page_stamp_vetoes keeps; never one after a dot
#                      leader (TOC page reference), a lone n-1 within 12 lines (figure / list markers)
#                      or next to another lone number line (table cell), which are content
#   page_footer_n_of_m a lone 'N/M' page footer (M <= 30)
#   underscore_rule    a run of 3+ '_' (fill-in line) replaced by a space
#   combining_mark     a stray combining mark (Mn) dropped
#   invisible_char     zero-width / soft hyphen / BOM removed
#   html_entity        an HTML character reference in raw decoded ('&amp;' -> '&')
# (v3: 'numero_fold' -- '№' / 'N°' / 'No. 5' written as 'nr. 5' -- is no longer allowed.)
ALLOWED = {"page_stamp_line", "page_footer_n_of_m", "underscore_rule", "combining_mark",
           "invisible_char", "html_entity"}
_ENTITY = re.compile(r"&?(?:[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]{1,7}|#\d{1,6}|#[xX][0-9A-Fa-f]{1,5});")
INVISIBLE = set("\u00ad\u200b\u200c\u200d\u200e\u200f\u2060\ufeff")


def _ws(s: str) -> str:
    return re.sub(r"\s+", "", s or "")


def _enum(lines: list[str]) -> set[int]:
    """Lone n within 12 lines after a lone n-1: an enumeration (figure markers), content."""
    cand = [(i, int(l)) for i, l in enumerate(lines) if LONE_NUM.fullmatch(l)]
    return {i for k, (i, n) in enumerate(cand) if k and cand[k - 1][1] == n - 1 and i - cand[k - 1][0] <= 12}


def _page_run(lines: list[str]) -> set[int]:
    cand = [(i, int(l)) for i, l in enumerate(lines) if LONE_NUM.fullmatch(l)]
    enum = _enum(lines)
    near = lambda a, b: 1 <= b[1] - a[1] <= 2 and 0 < b[0] - a[0] <= MAX_PAGE_LINES * (b[1] - a[1])
    out = set()
    for k, (i, n) in enumerate(cand):
        if i in enum:
            continue
        if (k and near(cand[k - 1], cand[k])) or (k + 1 < len(cand) and near(cand[k], cand[k + 1])):
            out.add(i)
    return out


COLUMN_GAP = 12  # v3.4, mirrors structure._COLUMN_GAP
MIN_PAGE_LINES = 5  # v3.4.1, mirrors structure._MIN_PAGE_LINES
PAGE_WORD_END = re.compile(r"(?:\bΣελ\.|\bσελ\.|\bΣελίδα|\bpp?\.|\bS\.|\bSeite|\bstr\.|\bpage)\s*$")  # v3.4.2
DOT_LEADER_ANY = re.compile(r"\.{2,}|…")  # v3.4.2
FOOTNOTE_REF = re.compile(r"([^\W\d_]{3,}|(?<!\d)[»”\"),;:!?])(\d{1,2})(?![^\W_])")  # v3.4.1
FOOTNOTE_LINE = re.compile(r"(\d{1,2})(?!(?:er|re|ère|ème|e|è|nd|st|rd|th|o|a|η|ος|ης|ου)\b)[^\W\d_]")  # v3.4.1
SIGN_PHRASE = re.compile(
    r"signal|panneau|limitation|limite|vitesse|km/h|schild|geschwindigkeit|höchst|\bsign\b|\blimit|speed"
    r"|značk|rýchlos|obmedzen|πινακίδ|σήμα|όριο|ταχύτ",
    re.IGNORECASE,
)  # v3.4.1
LIST_NEXT = re.compile(r"(?:[.)\]]|\(?(?:\d{1,3}|[^\W\d_]{1,4})[).](?:\s|$))")
_VETO_CACHE: dict = {}


def _page_stamp_vetoes(lines: list[str]) -> set[int]:
    """v3.4 / v3.4.1 / v3.4.2 (independent mirror of structure._page_stamp_vetoes; lines = stripped non-blank lines):
    lone numbers that are content, never page stamps."""
    key = id(lines)
    if key in _VETO_CACHE and _VETO_CACHE[key][0] is lines:
        return _VETO_CACHE[key][1]
    lone = [(k, int(l)) for k, l in enumerate(lines) if LONE_NUM.fullmatch(l)]
    last = len(lines) - 1
    out = set()
    notes = set()  # v3.4.1: footnote numbers referenced in the text
    for l in lines:
        notes |= {int(m.group(2)) for m in FOOTNOTE_REF.finditer(l) if not m.group(1)[0].isalpha() or m.group(1).islower()}
        m = FOOTNOTE_LINE.match(l)
        if m:
            notes.add(int(m.group(1)))
    for k, n in lone:
        before = [(kk, nn) for kk, nn in lone if 0 < k - kk <= MAX_PAGE_LINES]
        after = [(kk, nn) for kk, nn in lone if 0 < kk - k <= MAX_PAGE_LINES]
        prev = lines[k - 1] if k else ""
        nxt = lines[k + 1] if k < last else ""
        if (lines[k].startswith("0")
                or any(abs(kk - k) <= COLUMN_GAP for kk, _ in before + after)
                or (nxt and LIST_NEXT.match(nxt))
                or (k > 0 and not _ends_sentence(prev))
                or any(nn >= n for _, nn in before) or any(nn <= n for _, nn in after)
                or (2 <= n <= 9 and 0 < k < last and not any(n - 2 <= nn < n for _, nn in before))
                or n in notes
                or (n == 1 and k < last and not any(nn == 2 for _, nn in after))
                or (k > 0 and SIGN_PHRASE.search(prev))
                or k >= MAX_PAGE_LINES * n or (last + 1 >= MAX_PAGE_LINES and k < MIN_PAGE_LINES * (n - 1))
                or (k > 0 and (PAGE_WORD_END.search(prev) or DOT_LEADER_ANY.search(prev)))):  # v3.4.2: page reference
            out.add(k)
    _VETO_CACHE.clear(); _VETO_CACHE[key] = (lines, out)
    return out


def _lost_line_kind(lines: list[str], i: int, run: set[int]) -> str:
    l = lines[i]
    if LONE_NUM.fullmatch(l):
        prev = lines[i - 1] if i else ""
        nxt = lines[i + 1] if i + 1 < len(lines) else ""
        if i in _enum(lines) or re.search(r"(?:\.{2,}|…)\s*$", prev) or LONE_NUM.fullmatch(prev) or LONE_NUM.fullmatch(nxt):
            return "lost_lone_number"  # TOC page reference after a dot leader, or a table / figure cell: content
        if int(l) >= 1000 and i not in run:
            return "lost_lone_number"  # v3.2: map label / sheet number, not a page
        if i in _page_stamp_vetoes(lines):
            return "lost_lone_number"  # v3.4 / v3.4.1: column, list, phrase, order, paragraph, footnote, sign or position: content
        if not prev or _ends_sentence(prev):
            return "page_stamp_line"
        return "lost_lone_number"
    if N_OF_M.fullmatch(l):
        a, b = (int(x) for x in l.replace(" ", "").split("/"))
        if 1 <= a <= b <= 30:
            return "page_footer_n_of_m"
    if RULE_LINE.fullmatch(l):
        return "underscore_rule"
    if re.match(r"(?i)^(https?://|www\.)|@[\w-]+\.", l):
        return "lost_url_or_email"
    return "lost_line"


def _char_kind(a: str, b: str) -> str:
    """Classify one char-level edit raw 'a' -> IR 'b' (whitespace already removed)."""
    if not b and a and all(ch in INVISIBLE for ch in a):
        return "invisible_char"
    if not b and a and all(unicodedata.category(ch) == "Mn" for ch in a):
        return "combining_mark"
    if not b and re.fullmatch(r"_{3,}", a):
        return "underscore_rule"
    if _ENTITY.fullmatch(a) and html.unescape(a if a.startswith("&") else "&" + a) in (b, "&" + b, b + ";") \
            or (not b and _ENTITY.fullmatch(a) and html.unescape("&" + a.lstrip("&")) != "&" + a.lstrip("&")):
        return "html_entity"
    if re.fullmatch(r"(?i)(?:№|n\.?\s*[°º]|no\.?|n\.o)\.?", a) and b.lower() in ("nr.", "nr"):
        return "numero_fold"
    if not b and re.fullmatch(r"\.{4,}", a):
        return "dot_leader_removed"
    if a and b and re.sub(r"[\u2010-\u2015\u2212\ufe58\ufe63\uff0d]", "-", a) == b:
        return "dash_folded"
    if a and unicodedata.normalize("NFKC", a).replace(" ", "") == b:
        return "nfkc_folded"
    if "\u00b4" in a and a.replace("\u00b4", "") == b:
        return "accent_dropped"
    if a and not b:
        return "lost_chars"
    if b and not a:
        return "inserted_chars"
    return "changed_chars"


def classify(raw: str, body: str, pairs: collections.Counter | None = None) -> collections.Counter:
    """Classify every non-whitespace difference between raw and IR body (no folding)."""
    out: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()
    if _ws(raw) == _ws(body):
        return out
    raw_lines = [l.strip() for l in raw.splitlines() if l.strip()]
    body_lines = [l.strip() for l in body.splitlines() if l.strip()]
    run = _page_run(raw_lines)
    key = lambda l: re.sub(r"\s+", "", l)
    lm = difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, [key(l) for l in raw_lines], [key(l) for l in body_lines], autojunk=False)
    for lop, i1, i2, j1, j2 in lm.get_opcodes():
        if lop == "equal":
            continue
        a = "".join(key(l) for l in raw_lines[i1:i2])
        b = "".join(key(l) for l in body_lines[j1:j2])
        if a == b:
            continue
        if lop == "delete":
            for i in range(i1, i2):
                k = _lost_line_kind(raw_lines, i, run)
                out[k] += 1
                if pairs is not None:
                    prev = raw_lines[i - 1][-40:] if i else ""
                    pairs[(k, raw_lines[i][:60], "prev: " + prev)] += 1
            continue
        sm = difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, a, b, autojunk=False)
        for op, x1, x2, y1, y2 in sm.get_opcodes():
            if op == "equal":
                continue
            da, db = a[x1:x2], b[y1:y2]
            k = _char_kind(da, db)
            if k == "lost_chars" and (LONE_NUM.fullmatch(da) or N_OF_M.fullmatch(da)):
                # a whole lone-number / N-of-M line inside a changed block
                idx = [i for i in range(i1, i2) if key(raw_lines[i]) == da]
                k = _lost_line_kind(raw_lines, idx[0], run) if idx else k
            out[k] += 1
            if pairs is not None:
                pairs[(k, da[:40], db[:40])] += 1
    if not out:
        out["reordered_whitespace"] += 1
    return out


_BREAK_SPLIT = re.compile(r"\r\n|[\r\f\u2028\u2029]")


def _para_lines(text: str) -> tuple[list[str], list[bool], int]:
    """Non-blank lines (whitespace removed), 'blank-line run before this line' flags, and the
    longest run of consecutive blank lines between two non-blank lines."""
    keys, brk, pending, run, longest = [], [], False, 0, 0
    for ln in _BREAK_SPLIT.sub("\n", text or "").split("\n"):
        k = _ws(ln)
        if not k:
            if keys:
                pending, run = True, run + 1
            continue
        if pending:
            longest = max(longest, run)
        keys.append(k)
        brk.append(pending)
        pending, run = False, 0
    return keys, brk, longest


def paragraph_check(raw: str, body: str) -> collections.Counter:
    """Count paragraph-break outcomes raw -> IR body (see docstring item 5), aligned line by line."""
    c: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()
    b = body or ""
    if re.match(r"[ \t]*\n[ \t]*\n", b) or re.search(r"\n[ \t]*\n[ \t]*$", b):
        c["ir_edge_blank"] += 1
    rk, rb, _ = _para_lines(raw)
    ro = _orig_lines(raw)
    ik, ib, longest = _para_lines(b)
    if longest > 1:
        c["ir_multi_blank_run"] += 1
    c["raw_breaks"] += sum(rb)
    if not any(rb) and not any(ib):
        return c
    ops = [(0, len(rk), 0, len(ik), "equal")] if rk == ik else [
        (i1, i2, j1, j2, op) for op, i1, i2, j1, j2 in difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, rk, ik, autojunk=False).get_opcodes()]
    hit = set()
    for i1, i2, j1, j2, op in ops:
        for i in range(i1, i2):
            if not rb[i]:
                continue
            if op == "equal":
                j = j1 + i - i1
                if j == 0:  # every line before it was removed: no break left to keep
                    c["dropped_edge"] += 1
                    continue
                cand = [j] if ib[j] else []
            else:
                cand = [j for j in range(j1, min(j2 + 1, len(ik))) if ib[j]]
            free = [j for j in cand if j not in hit]
            if free:
                c["kept"] += 1
                hit.add(free[0])
            elif cand:
                c["merged"] += 1  # v3.2: 2 -> 1, a removed line sat between two blank-line runs
            elif _hyphen_join_ok(ro[i - 1][0], ro[i][0], True):
                c["hyphen_join"] += 1
            elif op != "equal" and (j1 == 0 or j1 >= len(ik)):
                c["dropped_edge"] += 1
            else:
                c["lost"] += 1
    c["invented"] += sum(1 for j, f in enumerate(ib) if f and j not in hit)
    c["ir_breaks"] += sum(ib)
    return c


def join_check(raw: str, body: str) -> collections.Counter:
    """v3.2: IR lines that are several raw lines glued together (characters all kept). Allowed only as a
    hyphenated word ('non-' + 'resident'); single letters, list markers and anything else are bad joins.
    Also counts IR lines split from one raw line (should be 0)."""
    c: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()
    ro = _orig_lines(raw)
    rk = [_ws(l) for l, _ in ro]
    ik = [_ws(l) for l in (body or "").splitlines() if _ws(l)]
    if rk == ik:
        return c
    for op, i1, i2, j1, j2 in difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, rk, ik, autojunk=False).get_opcodes():
        if op != "replace" or "".join(rk[i1:i2]) != "".join(ik[j1:j2]):
            continue
        # walk the raw lines and IR lines in step; a raw line boundary inside an IR line is a join
        pos, bounds, acc = 0, set(), 0
        for l in ik[j1:j2]:
            acc += len(l); bounds.add(acc)
        for k in range(i1, i2 - 1):
            pos += len(rk[k])
            if pos in bounds:
                continue
            if _hyphen_join_ok(ro[k][0], ro[k + 1][0], ro[k + 1][1]):
                c["hyphen_word_join"] += 1
            else:
                c["bad_join"] += 1
        rb = set(); acc = 0
        for l in rk[i1:i2]:
            acc += len(l); rb.add(acc)
        c["split_lines"] += sum(1 for x in sorted(bounds)[:-1] if x not in rb)
    return c


def run(pack: Path) -> dict:
    laws, articles, meta = load_local_source(pack)
    corpus, _ = build_corpus(laws, articles, meta)
    return compare(corpus, laws, articles, pack.name)


def run_hub(ir: str, raw_repo: str) -> dict:
    """Same checks against published data: IR corpus (repo@rev) vs raw (repo@rev) on the Hub."""
    import pandas as pd
    from huggingface_hub import HfApi, HfFileSystem
    fs = HfFileSystem()
    def files(spec, pat):
        repo, rev = spec.split("@")
        names = [s.rfilename for s in HfApi().dataset_info(repo, revision=rev).siblings]
        return [f"datasets/{repo}@{rev}/{f}" for f in sorted(names) if re.match(pat, f)]
    read = lambda paths, cols: pd.concat([pd.read_parquet(fs.open(p), columns=cols) for p in paths], ignore_index=True)
    if os.path.isdir(ir):  # a local release dir (pre-upload check)
        corpus = pd.concat([pd.read_parquet(p, columns=["source_id", "body", "source_url"])
                            for p in sorted(Path(ir).glob("data/corpus/*.parquet"))], ignore_index=True)
    else:
        corpus = read(files(ir, r"^data/corpus/.*\.parquet$"), ["source_id", "body", "source_url"])
    laws = read(files(raw_repo, r"^data/laws(?:-[\w-]+)?\.parquet$"), ["id", "text", "source_url"])
    arts = files(raw_repo, r"^data/articles(?:-[\w-]+)?\.parquet$")
    articles = read(arts, ["id", "text", "source_url"]) if arts else laws.iloc[0:0]
    res = compare(corpus, laws, articles, ir)
    res["expected_rows"] = int(len(laws) + len(articles))
    res["ok"] = res["ok"] and res["rows"] == res["expected_rows"]
    return res


def compare(corpus, laws, articles, name: str) -> dict:
    raw = {}
    for df in (laws, articles):
        for r in df[["id", "text", "source_url"]].itertuples(index=False):
            raw[str(r.id)] = (r.text or "", (r.source_url or "").strip())
    res = {"pack": name, "rows": int(len(corpus)), "raw_rows": len(raw),
           "source_url_missing": 0, "source_url_mismatch": 0,
           "date_wraps_raw": 0, "date_wraps_lost": 0, "date_wrap_examples": [],
           "rows_ws_equal": 0, "rows_differ": 0, "diff_categories": collections.Counter(),
           "rows_with_disallowed": 0, "disallowed_examples": [],
           "cases": {}, "cases_failed": 0, "paragraph_breaks": collections.Counter(),
           "paragraph_rows_bad": 0, "paragraph_bad_examples": [],
           "joins": collections.Counter(), "join_bad_examples": [], "underscore_rule_lines_removed": 0,
           "underscore_runs_removed": 0, "lost_content_lines": 0, "lost_content_examples": []}
    pairs: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()
    case_re = [(lid, re.compile(p)) for lid, p in CASES]
    seen = set()
    for row in corpus[["source_id", "body", "source_url"]].itertuples(index=False):
        sid = str(row.source_id)
        if sid not in raw:
            continue
        seen.add(sid)
        rtext, rurl = raw[sid]
        url = (row.source_url or "").strip()
        if rurl and not url:
            res["source_url_missing"] += 1
        elif rurl and url != rurl:
            res["source_url_mismatch"] += 1
        body = row.body or ""
        for m in DATE_WRAP.finditer(rtext):
            res["date_wraps_raw"] += 1
            if not re.search(re.escape(m.group(1)) + r"\s*" + m.group(2), body):
                res["date_wraps_lost"] += 1
                if len(res["date_wrap_examples"]) < 5:
                    res["date_wrap_examples"].append([sid, m.group(0)])
        for lid, rx in case_re:
            if sid == lid or sid.startswith(lid + "-art-"):
                n_raw = len(rx.findall(rtext))
                if n_raw:
                    n_ir = len(re.findall(rx.pattern.replace(r"\s*\n\s*", r"\s*"), body))
                    res["cases"][sid] = [n_raw, n_ir]
                    if n_ir < n_raw:
                        res["cases_failed"] += 1
        jc = join_check(rtext, body)
        res["joins"].update(jc)
        if (jc["bad_join"] or jc["split_lines"]) and len(res["join_bad_examples"]) < 8:
            res["join_bad_examples"].append([sid, dict(jc)])
        bl = collections.Counter(_ws(l) for l in body.splitlines() if _ws(l))
        for l in (x.strip() for x in rtext.splitlines()):
            if l and RULE_LINE.fullmatch(l) and not bl.get(_ws(l)):
                res["underscore_rule_lines_removed"] += 1
                res["underscore_runs_removed"] += len(re.findall(r"_{3,}", l))
        pc = paragraph_check(rtext, body)
        res["paragraph_breaks"].update(pc)
        if pc["lost"] or pc["invented"] or pc["ir_multi_blank_run"] or pc["ir_edge_blank"]:
            res["paragraph_rows_bad"] += 1
            if len(res["paragraph_bad_examples"]) < 8:
                res["paragraph_bad_examples"].append([sid, {k: v for k, v in pc.items() if k in ("lost", "invented", "ir_multi_blank_run", "ir_edge_blank")}])
        c = classify(rtext, body, pairs)
        if not c:
            res["rows_ws_equal"] += 1
            continue
        res["rows_differ"] += 1
        res["diff_categories"].update(c)
        bad = {k: v for k, v in c.items() if k not in ALLOWED}
        nl = sum(v for k, v in bad.items() if k.startswith("lost_") and k != "lost_chars")
        if nl:
            res["lost_content_lines"] += nl
            if len(res["lost_content_examples"]) < 8:
                res["lost_content_examples"].append([sid, {k: v for k, v in bad.items() if k.startswith("lost_")}])
        if bad:
            res["rows_with_disallowed"] += 1
            if len(res["disallowed_examples"]) < 8:
                res["disallowed_examples"].append([sid, bad])
    res["raw_rows_not_in_ir"] = len(set(raw) - seen)
    res["diff_categories"] = dict(res["diff_categories"])
    res["paragraph_breaks"] = dict(res["paragraph_breaks"])
    res["joins"] = dict(res["joins"])
    res["char_diffs"] = [[k, a, b, n] for (k, a, b), n in pairs.most_common(60)]
    res["cases_checked_rows"] = len(res["cases"])
    res["ok"] = (res["source_url_missing"] == 0 and res["source_url_mismatch"] == 0
                 and res["date_wraps_lost"] == 0 and res["rows_with_disallowed"] == 0
                 and res["raw_rows_not_in_ir"] == 0 and res["cases_failed"] == 0
                 and res["paragraph_rows_bad"] == 0
                 and res["joins"].get("bad_join", 0) == 0 and res["joins"].get("split_lines", 0) == 0
                 and res["lost_content_lines"] == 0
                 and (not any(r.startswith(lid) for r in raw for lid, _ in CASES) or res["cases_checked_rows"] > 0))
    return res


